 `POST /api/graph/import` feeds text or locally converted PDF Markdown into the same pipeline, without chat-message anchors. Before source registration or extraction, the route enforces the shared filename-extension list, recognizes PDFs by their `%PDF-` header, and refuses other files containing a zero byte in the first 8 KiB. Non-PDF files are decoded as UTF-8; the zero-byte rule is a limited binary-file heuristic, not complete text or encoding validation. The [import UI](../components/notes-import.tsx) queues one request per supported file, up to three in flight. Files are capped at 25 MiB; server aggregate file bytes per request are also capped at 25 MiB, with a 26 MiB multipart/proxy bound. PDF text comes from pdfjs (page Markdown) or MarkItDown; `.docx` files are converted with a Node DOCX reader. Image-only pages are reported and skipped unless the opt-in Baidu OCR switch is on, in which case PaddleOCR (local CLI) or the Baidu Cloud API fills just those pages; scanner caveats are still reported.
 
-Source identity hashes the original path/name; safe folder-relative paths can be supplied alongside matching filenames. Renaming or reorganizing a displayed source does not change its identity. PDF pages that are navigational back/front matter (a table-of-contents or index heading whose body is mostly entry lines) are dropped before joining, so they cost no extractor calls; an ambiguous page is kept. A completed import still processes the whole file, even unchanged text, and retry is not exactly-once processing. A stopped run is the one exception: `NotesSource.resume` records the chunking inputs' fingerprint and the leading chunks already merged, so re-uploading the same text at the same chunk budget resumes at the first unfinished chunk. A different text or chunk budget changes the fingerprint and starts from chunk 1; completing the run clears the checkpoint. Same-source overlap is refused as busy. Per-file outcomes distinguish completed, partial, failed, aborted, and busy; zero findings can still be a completed import.
+Source identity hashes the original path/name; safe folder-relative paths can be supplied alongside matching filenames. Renaming or reorganizing a displayed source does not change its identity. PDF navigation pages are dropped only when a contents/index heading is followed by at least three entries and every nonempty body line matches an entry; mixed or ambiguous pages are kept. The route checks the 1,000-page PDF limit before optional external conversion, applies enabled OCR before navigation classification, and classifies pages before stripping repeated headers. Whole-document MarkItDown output is used only when no navigation pages were removed and OCR recognized no pages, so it cannot restore skipped navigation or replace recognized scan text. A PDF with no content left after filtering is refused separately from an image-only PDF that needs OCR. A completed import still processes the whole file, even unchanged text, and retry is not exactly-once processing. A stopped run is the one exception: `NotesSource.resume` records the chunking inputs' fingerprint and the leading chunks already merged. Re-uploading the same text at the same chunk budget resumes at the first unfinished chunk. If all chunks merged before bookkeeping failed, retry repairs layout and can finish without calling the extractor again; the original bookkeeping failure is still reported. Invalid checkpoints are ignored without deleting source metadata or usage history. Changed text or chunk budget starts from chunk 1; completing the run clears the checkpoint. Same-source overlap is refused as busy. Per-file outcomes distinguish completed, partial, failed, aborted, and busy; zero findings can still be a completed import.
 
 `graph/source-organization.json` holds display overrides and folder placement, not original file contents. Folder imports reconstruct directories containing supported files. Organization is separate from session-sidebar placement. Both the chains browser and practice’s node picker hide practice-session source rows; this is a read projection, not deletion of conversations, graph contributions or placements. Folder selection excludes those hidden sources. Empty source names are muted in place, using full contents rather than search-filtered counts. Ordinary chains-view selection selects sources/folders, including descendants hidden by search; practice can select finer-grained graph material.
 
@@ -179,7 +179,7 @@ The **sensitive-path guard** refuses known private home locations, `.env` files,
 
 File/PDF/visual images share image postprocessing. Search supports Tavily, Brave, Exa, Firecrawl, and hosted Ollama adapters; page fetching is independent and does not need a search key. Dictation mints short-lived tokens server-side and streams audio browser → Deepgram. These external effects are not isolated by a scratch data directory alone.
 
-Research page/PDF fetches validate IP literals and every DNS candidate before connecting, then recheck the reported peer when available. Each new connection resolves and validates again; redirects pass through the same guard. This avoids relying on `remoteAddress`, which can be empty for configured sockets on Windows, without permitting private DNS results. TLS certificate and hostname validation remain enabled.
+Research page/PDF fetches validate IP literals and every DNS candidate before connecting, then recheck the reported peer when available. Private, link-local, and deprecated IPv6 site-local addresses are refused. Each new connection resolves and validates again; redirects pass through the same guard. This avoids relying on `remoteAddress`, which can be empty for configured sockets on Windows, without permitting private DNS results. TLS certificate and hostname validation remain enabled.
 
